#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:1
#: 5e3ece412fdc4b52b1f9951db79cb10a
msgid "Designing a Credible DEA Study: Who Can Learn from Whom?"
msgstr "设计一项可信的 DEA 研究：谁能向谁学习？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:3
#: beadf702c4b54891b579656a562962aa
msgid ""
"Imagine the first meeting of a regional health authority that wants to "
"compare hospitals. The spreadsheet appears reassuringly complete: staffing, "
"beds, treated cases, adverse events, teaching status, emergency obligations,"
" and characteristics of the local population. It would take only a few lines"
" of code to turn some of those columns into a DEA score."
msgstr ""
"设想某地区卫生主管部门第一次召开医院比较会议。眼前的电子表格看起来信息齐全：人员、床位、诊疗病例、不良事件、教学属性、急诊责任和当地人口特征。只需几行代码，就能把其中若干列变成"
" DEA 得分。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:9
#: d3893885c7c5473b86d9ff258cf9ca0e
msgid ""
"Yet the spreadsheet cannot decide what the authority means by performance. A"
" teaching hospital may appear to use too many resources because its training"
" mission was omitted. A rural hospital may appear inefficient because travel"
" time and minimum-service obligations were treated as managerial choices. A "
"hospital may appear to improve quality because an adverse event was entered "
"as an ordinary input, even though the study never explained how care and "
"harm are jointly produced. In each case the arithmetic can be faultless "
"while the economic comparison is wrong."
msgstr "然而，电子表格无法决定主管部门所说的绩效究竟是什么。教学医院可能因为培训任务被遗漏而显得资源使用过多；乡村医院可能因为通勤距离和最低服务责任被当成管理选择而显得低效率；如果把不良事件作为普通投入，医院也可能显得改善了质量，即使研究从未说明医疗服务与伤害如何联合产生。在每一种情形中，算术都可能完全正确，经济比较却是错的。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:18
#: ad315090bbe3450886d56b743a2af798
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The first task is therefore not to choose CCR, BCC, SBM, or another acronym."
" It is to define a comparison that an economist, manager, clinician, and "
"data owner would all recognize as the same study. Cook, Tone, and Zhu "
"describe this as work that must occur prior to choosing a DEA model; "
"practical DEA protocols likewise place unit definition, variable choice, "
"comparability, and sensitivity at the centre of the analysis "
"{cite:p}`cook2014model,dyson2001`."
msgstr ""
"因此，首要任务不是选择 CCR、BCC、SBM "
"或另一个缩写，而是界定一种经济学家、管理者、临床人员和数据所有者都会认作同一项研究的比较。Cook、Tone 与 Zhu 把这称为选择 DEA "
"模型之前必须完成的工作；实务 DEA 规范也把分析单元定义、变量选择、可比性和敏感性置于分析中心 "
"{cite:p}`cook2014model,dyson2001`。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:26
#: a758dda12775407aae55b20ae508064f
msgid ""
"Before the first model is fitted, the researcher should be able to explain "
"in ordinary organizational language what each hospital is responsible for, "
"what it must preserve, what it could reasonably change over the stated "
"horizon, and which other hospitals provide relevant evidence. These "
"judgments define the performance question. The later optimization makes "
"their implications explicit; it cannot make the judgments on the "
"researcher's behalf."
msgstr "拟合第一个模型之前，研究者应能用通常的组织语言解释每家医院对什么负责、必须保留什么、在声明的期限内可以合理改变什么，以及哪些医院提供相关证据。这些判断界定绩效问题；后续优化只是明确其含义，不能代替研究者作出判断。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 8c678777983a4c19a7ee4e07cafc3c67
msgid ""
"Purpose and commitments, organizational responsibility and time, and "
"comparable evidence shape a study design that produces a performance "
"finding, operating evidence, and a bounded conclusion"
msgstr "目的与承诺、组织责任与时间以及可比证据共同塑造研究设计，继而产生绩效结论、经营证据与有边界的解释"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:38
#: 2955d51cd89d46d5b425ee84ccf5829d
msgid ""
"A defensible study moves from the organization's purpose and production "
"boundary to an explicit comparison design. Scores and targets emerge from "
"that design; they cannot substitute for it."
msgstr "一项可辩护的研究，应从组织目的与生产边界走向明确的比较设计。得分和目标方案由这一设计产生，不能取代它。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:43
#: 1e58ab6484ec4565910c76c6305cc482
msgid "Begin with the decision the organization actually faces"
msgstr "从组织真正面对的决定出发"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:45
#: 381e1f83e2d9413b947733f3bfc4d85b
msgid ""
"Suppose the authority's immediate question concerns annual resource "
"stewardship in district general hospitals:"
msgstr "假设主管部门眼下关心地区综合医院的年度资源受托责任："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:48
#: c171969da4a94d94bc221f072dc384b8
msgid ""
"Could each hospital have delivered its risk-adjusted volume of completed "
"care with fewer controllable clinical resources, relative to hospitals with "
"a comparable service mandate?"
msgstr "相对于服务任务可比的医院，每家医院能否用更少的可控临床资源，完成其经过风险调整的既定诊疗量？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:52
#: 614e1d2fd4854af8ae524ac2390ac492
msgid ""
"Every phrase in this question restricts the claim the authority will later "
"be entitled to make."
msgstr "这句话中的每个短语都限制主管部门以后有权作出的主张。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:55
#: b121c7ba6c8f4ef593838a269da69bf0
msgid ""
"The hospital site, rather than an individual department, is provisionally "
"the organization whose stewardship is being evaluated."
msgstr "暂时以整个医院院区为受评价的资源管理组织，而不是某个单独部门。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:57
#: f43b75508e48494f9becf15ba223db91
msgid ""
"Completed care is a service commitment to be protected rather than an amount"
" the authority is presently asking hospitals to reduce."
msgstr "既定诊疗是需要保护的服务承诺，而不是主管部门当前要求医院削减的数量。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:59
#: b3128049c00a43a685a04b4349ea7b9e
msgid ""
"Clinical resources are treated as quantities that management could adjust "
"over the stated horizon."
msgstr "临床资源被视为管理者可以在给定期限内调整的数量。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:61
#: 717e5a5b5783486da46dba80fd830ce6
msgid "The evidence must come from hospitals with comparable service mandates."
msgstr "证据必须来自服务任务可比的医院。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:62
#: e0cef3dad50846d5bbeea79cbecc7a02
msgid ""
"The result is a relative operating benchmark, not an estimate of the effect "
"of a management intervention."
msgstr "结果是相对经营标杆，不是某项管理干预效果的估计。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:65
#: 8a81f983c99846edbd51cfa37fe8ade0
msgid ""
"Change the board's decision and the study changes. A short-run staffing "
"review may hold installed beds fixed. A capacity plan may allow staffing to "
"adjust while asking what those beds could support. A quality programme may "
"seek more completed care and fewer adverse events together. A service "
"redesign may need to open the hospital and represent intake, diagnosis, "
"treatment, and follow-up as connected processes. These are different "
"economic accounts of what the organization can change and what society asks "
"it to deliver; they are not alternative wordings of one score."
msgstr "董事会的决定一变，研究也随之改变。短期人员审查可能固定已安装床位；产能规划可能允许调整人员，同时询问这些床位能支持多少服务；质量计划可能希望同时增加既定诊疗并减少不良事件；服务重构则可能需要打开医院这一黑箱，把接诊、诊断、治疗和随访表示为相互连接的过程。这些是组织可以改变什么、社会要求其提供什么的不同经济核算，不是同一个得分的不同说法。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:74
#: c3ec36b498bb4913a8923ff8ba284633
msgid ""
"The decision horizon matters as much as the organizational purpose. Beds may"
" be fixed during next month's rostering exercise but adjustable in a ten-"
"year capital plan. A minimum emergency service may be a binding obligation "
"for the current contract but negotiable in a future commissioning round. "
"Calling a quantity “controllable” without naming the responsible decision "
"maker and time horizon leaves the performance question unfinished. DEA does "
"not discover managerial discretion from the data: it evaluates the "
"discretion that the study has declared."
msgstr ""
"决策期限与组织目的同样重要。床位在下个月的排班中可能固定，在十年资本规划中却可以调整；最低急诊服务可能是当前合同中的硬约束，也可能在未来委托谈判中重新协商。如果不说明责任决策者和时间范围，就把某个数量称为“可控”，绩效问题仍不完整。DEA"
" 不从数据中发现管理权限，而是评价研究已经声明的权限。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:83
#: c75449ba4ecb43208756426311b8b34d
msgid "Where does one hospital begin and end?"
msgstr "一家医院的边界从哪里开始，到哪里结束？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:85
#: 27859cdcb621403085bb79532ce5b512
msgid ""
"The decision-making unit, or DMU, is an economic boundary rather than merely"
" a row label. It identifies the organization, activity, or operating history"
" to which resources and services will be attributed. Ideally that boundary "
"also matches a meaningful locus of responsibility: someone should be able to"
" explain the operating choices represented inside it. For the health "
"authority, “hospital” could mean at least four different things:"
msgstr ""
"决策单元（decision-making "
"unit，DMU）是一条经济边界，不只是行标签。它界定资源和服务归属于哪个组织、活动或经营历程。理想情况下，这条边界还应对应有意义的责任主体：有人能够解释边界内部所代表的经营选择。对卫生主管部门而言，“医院”至少可以有四种含义："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 068af6155a27423588bcb45857c12d52
msgid "Possible unit"
msgstr "可能的分析单元"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: cdfa3427041c4260b626d07443ad0ea5
msgid "What lies inside the production account"
msgstr "生产核算包含什么"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: d503fa1c29b84f3280f201e04b33ffe0
msgid "Question it could support"
msgstr "能够支持的问题"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 37013c556fd04dfc867f9b1537899bd7
msgid "complete hospital site"
msgstr "完整医院院区"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 23a215a6079b4f188ecd829817920a2a
msgid "all represented clinical resources and final care outcomes"
msgstr "所代表的全部临床资源与最终医疗结果"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 66679a2f02ec460cb5b0f833cbf90bbf
msgid "overall site resource stewardship"
msgstr "院区整体的资源受托责任"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 091923b4e0f94beca5eed70c9f6acaec
msgid "clinical pathway"
msgstr "临床路径"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: a679787d8fbd4967b1e74148b1e77d8f
msgid "intake, diagnosis, treatment, and follow-up for a defined patient group"
msgstr "针对特定患者群体的接诊、诊断、治疗与随访"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: b950ebf2496947c6b114d72889004db8
msgid "pathway performance across organizational departments"
msgstr "跨组织部门的路径绩效"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 8e1646737ff94eca91b7eb9bcc7ffa05
msgid "hospital-year"
msgstr "医院—年度"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 9a0926bf0f154a3990054f392ec606e5
msgid "one site's resources and services during one reporting period"
msgstr "一个院区在一个报告期内的资源和服务"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: e0ac9f4b1d64438dba1426c306b1d378
msgid ""
"contemporaneous efficiency; a linked panel of comparable hospital-years can "
"support productivity change"
msgstr "当期效率；由可比医院—年度组成的相互联结面板可以支持生产率变化"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: b0997bd0cf6e4f1c87237659d04072bd
msgid "hospital trajectory"
msgstr "医院轨迹"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 515fbe38e2ea4a489bbd98f5af9faa93
msgid "several years joined by capacity, waiting lists, or other inherited states"
msgstr "通过产能、候诊名单或其他继承状态连接的多年经营"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 649a00feaaf8442c870e2ac196f98e41
msgid "performance of one intertemporally feasible operating history"
msgstr "一条跨期可行经营历程的绩效"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:99
#: 1f884b56ca484d1cab4293f870925ddf
msgid ""
"The choice determines what counts as an input, output, internal handoff, or "
"state. A legal entity is not automatically the right production boundary. If"
" laboratory services are purchased from another organization, their cost or "
"quantity should not disappear simply because the laboratory is outside the "
"hospital's legal boundary. If one hospital records referred patients as "
"completed episodes while another removes them from both resources and "
"outcomes, their rows do not describe the same production unit."
msgstr "这种选择决定什么算投入、产出、内部交接或状态。法律实体不会自动成为正确的生产边界。如果检验服务向外部机构购买，其成本或数量不能仅因实验室位于医院法律边界之外就消失。如果一家医院把转诊患者记为已完成病例，另一家却同时从资源和结果中剔除这些患者，两行数据描述的就不是同一种生产单元。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:107
#: 745705bb32d74cb78798536039271e2c
msgid ""
"Good boundaries also prevent double counting. A diagnostic result can be a "
"final service in a diagnostic-centre study. Inside a complete hospital "
"pathway it may instead be an intermediate service handed to treatment. A "
"waiting list can be an undesirable end-of-year burden in one static account,"
" but when the same cases become next year's opening obligation it is more "
"naturally represented as a carry-over. The spreadsheet value has not "
"changed; its economic role has. The same quantity should not be rewarded "
"once as an internal handoff and again as final care unless the production "
"account can justify both roles."
msgstr "合理的边界还可以防止重复计算。诊断结果在诊断中心研究中可以是最终服务；在完整医院路径中，它可能只是交给治疗过程的中间服务。候诊名单在静态核算中可以是年末非合意负担；当同一批病例成为下一年的期初责任时，更自然的角色是结转变量。电子表格中的数值没有改变，经济角色却变了。除非生产核算能够为两种角色同时辩护，同一数量不能先作为内部交接得到一次奖励，再作为最终医疗服务得到一次奖励。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:117
#: b59210977c094b789e6c74a8ee93898d
msgid ""
"For repeated observations, the identity rule must be equally clear. A "
"hospital merger, split, service transfer, or coding-system change may break "
"the continuity of the apparent hospital name. A mechanical match of "
"identical labels can therefore compare different organizational entities. "
"Conversely, a renamed hospital may remain the same production unit. The "
"researcher needs an economic continuity rule, not just a text-matching rule."
msgstr "对重复观测，还必须明确身份延续规则。医院合并、拆分、服务转移或编码系统变化，都可能打破表面医院名称的连续性。机械匹配相同标签，可能比较两个不同组织实体；反过来，改名后的医院也可能仍是同一生产单元。研究者需要经济连续性规则，而不只是文本匹配规则。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:124
#: 5a3b4a3de40e44b898d8134c9e6730ba
msgid "A column acquires meaning from the production story"
msgstr "数据列的含义来自生产故事"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:126
#: d648d89f2c044d39ae974c6928afb3e7
msgid ""
"Once the unit is defined, each column must be assigned an economic role "
"within that boundary and horizon. For hospital $j$, the book writes "
"resources as $x_j$, desirable services and outcomes as $y_j$, and jointly "
"produced burdens as $b_j$. These symbols do not classify a column by its "
"name or by whether a large value looks attractive. They record the role that"
" the study can defend."
msgstr ""
"分析单元确定后，每一列都必须在该边界和期限内被赋予经济角色。对于医院 $j$，本书以 $x_j$ 表示资源，$y_j$ 表示合意服务与结果，$b_j$ "
"表示联合生产的负担。这些符号不会按列名分类，也不会按“大数值看起来是否可取”分类，而是记录研究能够辩护的角色。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:132
#: b3219a5a47f84c0495cdc11c998c8d2c
msgid "Consider the variables available for the hospital study."
msgstr "考虑医院研究中可获得的变量。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: db7f07e4a973438eab2db930e9d771fb
msgid "Recorded quantity"
msgstr "记录数量"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: ba47310d36c343fa836682e4d280f526
msgid "Plausible role in the annual study"
msgstr "年度研究中可能的角色"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 6ef5f8f5818448e79bb00aa1a638e903
msgid "Question that must be settled first"
msgstr "必须先解决的问题"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: ca9927e641e34fefa1c206d4535be2df
msgid "clinical staff hours"
msgstr "临床人员工时"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 132a9f0ea9444599b2fc9f1f6997e2b3
msgid "controllable input"
msgstr "可控投入"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: a7bc5a0095804e46837c5e2e302cc27d
msgid "Are agency and contracted hours measured on the same basis at every site?"
msgstr "各院区是否按同一口径计量派遣人员和合同人员工时？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 0066a0af68f547a38ec8900ca0da58a5
msgid "staffed bed-days"
msgstr "实际开放床日"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 5357c4deeee24fcc990d7f3b10951882
msgid "input or quasi-fixed resource"
msgstr "投入或准固定资源"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 9bdc029300874c8ebfff11cf2157332f
msgid "Can management alter staffed capacity over the stated horizon?"
msgstr "管理者能否在给定期限内调整开放床位能力？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: f22379852a9a452e9ca338435a8d95d9
msgid "risk-adjusted completed episodes"
msgstr "风险调整后的既定病例"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 9ea30ea9f70042518567918f6a90adfb
msgid "desirable output"
msgstr "合意产出"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 63b19bdcf9d34c5bba28efb8e760f17c
msgid ""
"Does the adjustment preserve comparable definitions of severity and "
"completion?"
msgstr "调整是否保持了病情严重程度与病例完成定义的可比性？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: a72189239a80493580dc693915aefe60
msgid "avoidable inpatient harm events"
msgstr "可避免的住院伤害事件"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 8d6fd3067f6a4f97b4f453195b9f8d2e
msgid "undesirable output"
msgstr "非合意产出"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: fdc841d3f6d64630bf5ece84b935c94b
msgid ""
"Is harm jointly generated within the hospital boundary, and how may it be "
"reduced?"
msgstr "伤害是否在医院边界内联合产生，又允许以何种方式减少？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 2c6891afb8b14143a9b69e9b305eaf79
msgid "teaching mandate"
msgstr "教学任务"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: c68b1fbbf8aa4f878fd0b6d775f87353
msgid "mission or operating condition"
msgstr "组织使命或经营条件"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 610d59301598449a82936144b810dc9c
msgid ""
"Is training itself a measured output, or does the mandate define a different"
" comparison group?"
msgstr "培训本身是一项可测量产出，还是教学任务界定了不同的比较群体？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 04dabd310d0442b3ad3801e6ed5d558f
msgid "population deprivation"
msgstr "当地人口贫困程度"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 2e553873bc114768bc8adb88251c9da4
msgid "contextual condition"
msgstr "情境条件"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: b2d8e67741954cef8808125bdbd09da1
msgid ""
"Does it change attainable care opportunities, and is it outside hospital "
"control?"
msgstr "它是否改变可实现医疗机会，又是否不受医院控制？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 113404c13d9048af899d00de18c5c407
msgid "rural travel time"
msgstr "乡村地区通勤时间"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 7f0982687ceb42f785708cd56d815b5d
msgid "operating environment"
msgstr "经营环境"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 3fa350af44f845238450c311112ed08c
msgid ""
"Does remoteness impose a minimum-service configuration or a distinct "
"technology?"
msgstr "偏远是否带来最低服务配置或不同的生产技术？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: 7f6b056233db46e8bb25c53066034c17
msgid "year-end waiting list"
msgstr "年末候诊名单"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: fd33f1d1283b440a98c3db9977e1f0f4
msgid "final burden or intertemporal state"
msgstr "最终负担或跨期状态"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:33
#: edc2f643f2ba4c87bf3e61c774933e44
msgid "Is the study static, or does today's backlog become tomorrow's obligation?"
msgstr "研究是静态的，还是今天的积压会成为明天的责任？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:145
#: 55b135563ba14576bf6646f5ea82ba74
msgid "Four distinctions are especially important."
msgstr "其中四项区别尤其重要。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:147
#: afa0dacf05614944a3a4c9dc3c788a3b
msgid ""
"First, an input is a resource used within the declared production boundary, "
"not simply a variable that management would like to reduce. A subsidy, a "
"deprivation index, or a statutory obligation may affect the organization's "
"opportunities without being a consumed resource. An input-oriented question "
"also implies that the represented input can be adjusted over the stated "
"horizon; otherwise the study should preserve it or describe its restricted "
"role explicitly."
msgstr "第一，投入是已声明生产边界内使用的资源，不只是管理者希望减少的变量。补贴、贫困指数或法定责任可能影响组织的机会，却不是生产中消耗的资源。投入导向问题还意味着在给定期限内可以调整所表示的投入；否则，研究应保护它，或明确描述其受限角色。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:155
#: 8b3ed560e54f4f59ae56fe91cdd022a8
msgid ""
"Second, a desirable output is something the production account values as "
"delivered, not simply a column whose larger numbers look favourable. "
"Unadjusted treatment counts can reward low-complexity case selection. "
"Quality indicators and case-mix adjustment need clinical and measurement "
"justification before they become production quantities. An output should "
"represent a service or outcome for which the DMU can meaningfully be held "
"responsible, rather than a distant social outcome driven mainly by forces "
"outside its boundary."
msgstr ""
"第二，合意产出是生产核算认可为已经提供的服务或结果，不只是数值越大看起来越好的列。未调整的诊疗量可能奖励选择低复杂度病例。质量指标和病例组合调整必须先有临床与测量依据，才能成为生产数量。产出应代表"
" DMU 可以被合理要求负责的服务或结果，而不是主要由边界外力量决定的遥远社会结果。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:164
#: 717c79dbbf9b401e80f17e400f8dee93
msgid ""
"Third, an undesirable output is not an ordinary input with an inconvenient "
"sign. Harm occurs with the delivery of care and may require resources, "
"foregone activity, or process redesign to reduce. A study that includes harm"
" must choose an explicit undesirable-output production account. Part III "
"develops several such accounts because different mechanisms imply different "
"attainable improvements."
msgstr "第三，非合意产出不是符号不方便的普通投入。伤害伴随医疗服务产生，削减伤害可能需要资源、牺牲活动或重新设计过程。纳入伤害的研究必须选择明确的非合意产出生产核算。第三篇发展多种此类核算，因为不同机制意味着不同的可实现改进。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:171
#: 782f861292e547f0a1d783db9ef18e69
msgid ""
"Fourth, an uncontrollable environment is not automatically a non-"
"discretionary input. Deprivation, remoteness, regulation, and teaching "
"status can affect comparison opportunities without being resources consumed "
"in production. Entering them mechanically as inputs can reward an "
"organization for “using more” of an adverse condition and may assert a "
"monotonic production relation that has no economic basis. Possible responses"
" include a defensible peer screen, declared groups and a metafrontier, "
"conditional frontier methods, or a separate contextual analysis. They answer"
" different questions and should not be chosen after seeing which gives the "
"preferred ranking. The governing question is whether the condition changes "
"the attainable opportunity set, the organization's distance from a shared "
"opportunity set, or only the interpretation of the result. Those claims "
"require different designs."
msgstr "第四，不可控环境不会自动成为非任意投入。贫困、偏远、监管和教学属性可以影响比较机会，却不是生产中消耗的资源。机械地把它们作为投入，可能因组织“使用更多”不利条件而奖励它，并主张一种没有经济依据的单调生产关系。可能的处理包括有依据的比较对象筛选、预先声明群组与共同前沿、条件前沿方法，或单独的情境分析。它们回答不同问题，不能在看到哪个方法产生理想排名后再选择。关键要问：条件改变的是可实现机会集合、组织相对于共同机会集合的距离，还是只改变结果解释？这些主张需要不同设计。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:185
#: d5d27c23cb514259b09337afa83c9e9a
msgid ""
"Ratios require the same discipline. A harm rate combines a numerator and an "
"exposure denominator. Treating the rate as though it were a freely "
"disposable quantity can imply operating plans that do not correspond to any "
"attainable combination of events and cases. When possible, keep the "
"underlying quantities and the exposure account visible. Prices, "
"expenditures, and physical quantities also answer different questions: "
"replacing staff hours with wage cost, for example, changes a resource-use "
"comparison into a value account that also reflects local prices."
msgstr "比率也需要同样的约束。伤害率把分子与暴露分母结合起来；把比率当作可自由处置的数量，可能产生并不对应任何可实现事件—病例组合的经营方案。只要可能，就应保留基础数量和暴露核算。价格、支出与实物数量同样回答不同问题：例如用工资成本替代人员工时，会把资源使用比较变成同时反映当地价格的价值核算。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:194
#: d206d21500ef45bca8570836d07c5659
msgid ""
"Measurement comparability is part of economic comparability. Two hospitals "
"do not supply the same evidence if “completed episode” means discharge at "
"one site and referral at another, if one resource is a stock and the other "
"an annual flow, or if nominal expenditure spans years with different price "
"levels. Units, coverage, accounting period, case-mix adjustment, and "
"missing-data treatment must be reconciled before the rows can be interpreted"
" as operating plans in a common production account."
msgstr "测量可比性是经济可比性的一部分。如果“既定病例”在一家医院表示出院，在另一家表示转诊；如果一种资源是存量，另一种是年度流量；或者名义支出跨越价格水平不同的年份，那么两家医院提供的就不是相同证据。单位、覆盖范围、会计期间、病例组合调整和缺失数据处理，都必须在各行可被解释为共同生产核算中的经营方案之前统一。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:202
#: 73cb38c1e5c9489c961b5c46b49375f5
msgid "Comparison eligibility is an institutional claim"
msgstr "比较资格是一项制度主张"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:204
#: ec7fb1f1ef8b4adc86ac923dc86b333f
msgid ""
"DEA learns from represented operating practices. Before asking which "
"combination of those practices could support a benchmark, the study must "
"decide which observations are institutionally and economically eligible to "
"teach the focal hospital. This is not a housekeeping choice. It determines "
"the opportunity set against which performance will be read."
msgstr ""
"DEA "
"从被代表的经营实践中学习。在询问这些实践的哪种组合能够支持标杆之前，研究必须决定哪些观测在制度和经济上有资格向焦点医院提供借鉴。这不是数据整理选择，而是决定绩效所依据生产机会集合的实质决定。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:210
#: 3403134dc1f24419bf0bc0655b9110f9
msgid ""
"Consider a separate teaching case. Lakeside is an urban district general "
"hospital without a tertiary trauma mandate. The authority's first "
"comparison-eligibility ledger might read:"
msgstr "考虑另一个教学案例。Lakeside 是一家没有三级创伤任务的城市地区综合医院。主管部门最初的比较资格台账可以写成："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:218
#: 71e8df869f3841668e14b1515d5f9967
msgid "Candidate"
msgstr "候选对象"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:219
#: 37961cf010de479a8d25a4f9bde29de3
msgid "Institutional and measurement record"
msgstr "制度与测量记录"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:220
#: c4328cccdf864a2eb7da0860224825d6
msgid "Eligibility decision"
msgstr "资格决定"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:221
#: aab6bbcc20524567a76142b513d799cb
msgid "Lakeside"
msgstr "Lakeside"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:222
#: 909ec15ce6cd4bc7a59e23af282565e9
msgid "focal district hospital; standard service contract; common coding protocol"
msgstr "焦点地区医院；标准服务合同；共同编码规范"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:223
#: 833fac83e4a34810bcd56027ea8b6c9d
msgid ""
"include under both declared rules; ordinary self-inclusive DEA retains the "
"focal observation"
msgstr "在两项已声明规则下均纳入；通常包含自身的 DEA 保留焦点观测"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:225
#: 29689c635a47418c8a52b57bcf030ee5
msgid "North and East"
msgstr "North 与 East"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:226
#: dc21325952f84cdd9607b4da6934e9c9
msgid ""
"district hospitals; same standard contract, service boundary, and coding "
"protocol"
msgstr "地区医院；相同的标准合同、服务边界与编码规范"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:228
#: 6593a3486029453c8930f68e282153d7
msgid "include under both declared rules"
msgstr "在两项已声明规则下均纳入"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:229
#: ed30ee6eba0241d3b625a67c1e1ad147
msgid "West"
msgstr "West"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:230
#: fbc1351222374d86a64e6b21fa3f0901
msgid ""
"district hospital with audited definitions but an integrated urgent-care "
"contract"
msgstr "定义已经审计，但采用综合急诊合同的地区医院"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:232
#: 8a74595ec5bd4ba5bce431d7aee89156
msgid ""
"include only under the broader district-mission rule, and only if prior "
"institutional evidence supports transferability"
msgstr "仅在较宽的地区任务规则下纳入，且事先必须有制度证据支持可迁移性"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:234
#: 8f469d52038b4b788d47d820780720f0
msgid "Riverside"
msgstr "Riverside"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:235
#: a28a12575db74c1da92ec4f1bf6f2e60
msgid ""
"district hospital serving a remote population under minimum-service "
"obligations"
msgstr "服务偏远人口、负有最低服务责任的地区医院"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:237
#: 8c57de5d0d8641ceb8f0717a7fd037ca
msgid "exclude from both rules; reserve for an environment-sensitivity comparison"
msgstr "两项规则均排除；保留用于环境敏感性比较"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:238
#: c1d300d240a84e7eac133da913a4b558
msgid "University"
msgstr "University"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:239
#: f57d309922224dcfb4395d5df3c23b62
msgid "tertiary referral, research, teaching, and major-trauma mandates"
msgstr "承担三级转诊、科研、教学和重大创伤任务"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:240
#: 9d9002a2701d4dc4ae6d49fe54706977
msgid "exclude from both district-hospital populations"
msgstr "从两个地区医院总体中排除"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:241
#: 90402d1a4e6e4b32b8b4fc4b64be3df6
msgid "South"
msgstr "South"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:242
#: cdfa9ff006474de3b91f02e74f3f24e6
msgid "nominally comparable, but uses an unreconciled episode definition"
msgstr "名义上可比，但采用尚未统一的病例定义"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:243
#: 279b320a61ce4d238989ca7ed6e2a577
msgid "exclude until the data audit is resolved"
msgstr "排除，直至完成数据审计"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:246
#: 475bdfa4171545919dac493a2bfbf6c5
msgid ""
"Exclusion is not a judgment that Riverside, University, or South is poorly "
"managed. It says that these two studies cannot use their records as evidence"
" of what Lakeside could attain under the declared mandate and measurement "
"system. Riverside may belong in a grouped or conditional comparison. "
"University may require teaching and tertiary outputs, or a separate "
"technology. South presents a data problem, not a technology group. West "
"poses a different question: does its integrated urgent-care contract change "
"the production opportunity relevant to Lakeside, or is the difference "
"compatible with learning across a shared district mission? Institutional "
"evidence, not a preferred score, must answer that question."
msgstr ""
"排除 Riverside、University 或 South，并不表示它们管理不善，而是表示这两项研究不能把它们的记录用作 "
"Lakeside 在已声明任务与测量体系下能够实现什么的证据。Riverside 可以进入分组或条件比较；University "
"可能需要纳入教学与三级服务产出，或采用不同技术；South 是数据问题，不是技术群组。West 提出另一问题：其综合急诊合同是否改变与 Lakeside"
" 有关的生产机会，还是两者差异仍允许在共同地区任务下学习？应由制度证据回答，而不是由偏好的得分回答。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:257
#: 217a255a79c3466bbd7352f9550b2366
msgid ""
"The rules should be stated before scores are inspected. Removing an "
"inconvenient peer after it creates a demanding benchmark changes the "
"economic question and the estimated frontier at the same time. A useful "
"study record therefore retains every observation considered, its eligibility"
" decision, the reason for that decision, and the institutional or empirical "
"evidence on which it rests. A sensitivity analysis may compare two "
"defensible rules, but it should not reverse-engineer a rule from the desired"
" ranking."
msgstr "规则应在查看得分之前声明。某个比较对象形成严格标杆后，因为不方便而将其删除，会同时改变经济问题与估计前沿。有用的研究记录应保留每项曾被考虑的观测、资格决定及理由，以及决定所依据的制度或经验证据。敏感性分析可以比较两项可辩护规则，却不能从理想排名倒推规则。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:265
#: 742ff591d45d4ff3873dcd45b3e61841
msgid ""
"Three groups of organizations must now be kept separate. The **candidate "
"roster** contains every record examined during the data and institutional "
"audit. The **eligible reference population** contains only the records that "
"pass the rule declared for the study. The model then selects an **active "
"peer plan** from that eligible population: only observations with positive "
"fitted intensities contribute to the selected comparator. Eligibility is "
"therefore an analyst's prior institutional decision; active peers are a "
"result. An eligible hospital need not become an active peer, and the "
"optimization cannot rescue a hospital that the study has already declared "
"ineligible."
msgstr "现在必须分开三类组织。**候选名单**包含数据与制度审计中检查的所有记录；**合格参照总体**只包含通过研究已声明规则的记录；模型随后从合格总体中选择**活跃参照方案**，只有拟合强度为正的观测参与所选比较。因此，资格是分析者事先作出的制度决定，活跃参照单元则是结果。合格医院不一定成为活跃参照单元，优化模型也不能重新纳入已经被研究判为不合格的医院。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:275
#: 257eed2ed0a04cd9941ae3c4a5cc59e2
msgid ""
"In the unified notation, only eligible observations enter the reference "
"matrices $X$, $Y$, and, when burdens are represented, $B$. For the focal "
"hospital $o$, positive values of $\\lambda_j$ identify the eligible "
"hospitals that contribute to the selected comparator plan. A zero "
"$\\lambda_j$ does not mean that hospital $j$ was irrelevant to the study: "
"its presence may still shape the frontier or become active for another "
"hospital. Nor does a positive $\\lambda_j$ prove that its practices are "
"transferable. It says only that its represented resource--service bundle "
"contributes to this model-supported comparison."
msgstr ""
"在统一符号中，只有合格观测进入参照矩阵 $X$、$Y$，以及表示负担时的 $B$。对焦点医院 $o$，正的 "
"$\\lambda_j$ 标示参与所选比较方案的合格医院。零值 $\\lambda_j$ 不表示医院 $j$ "
"与研究无关：它仍可能塑造前沿，或成为其他医院的活跃参照单元。正的 $\\lambda_j$ "
"也不能证明其实践可迁移，只表示其被代表的资源—服务组合参与了模型支持的比较。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:285
#: e5c24af1865540caa8a0524f579f6598
msgid ""
"The distinction becomes visible if the authority holds Lakeside's recorded "
"operation fixed and states two policies before fitting the model. A strict "
"same-contract rule admits Lakeside, North, and East. It gives Lakeside an "
"input-oriented VRS radial score of 0.9375, with North supplying the selected"
" active peer evidence. Suppose the authority also adopts a broader district-"
"mission rule after documenting an ex-ante institutional-comparability "
"review. That rule admits West. Lakeside's score becomes 0.9028, supported by"
" a fitted plan combining North and West. Nothing about Lakeside's recorded "
"resources or completed care changed; the admitted evidence changed. In "
"management terms, the two scores represent common proportional resource-"
"saving opportunities of 6.25 percent and 9.72 percent, respectively, while "
"protecting the recorded completed-care commitment and before any slack "
"completion."
msgstr ""
"如果主管部门固定 Lakeside 的观测经营方案，并在拟合模型前声明两项政策，这一区别就很直观。严格的同合同规则纳入 Lakeside、North 与"
" East，得到 Lakeside 投入导向 VRS 径向得分 0.9375，North "
"提供所选活跃参照证据。假设主管部门还在事前完成制度可比性审查后采用较宽的地区任务规则，纳入 West；Lakeside 得分变为 0.9028，由 "
"North 与 West 的拟合组合支持。Lakeside 的资源和既定诊疗记录没有改变，改变的是被允许进入比较的证据。从管理角度看，两项得分分别表示 "
"6.25% 与 9.72% 的共同比例资源节约机会，同时保护记录的既定诊疗量，并且均未完成松弛调整。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:299
#: 5317bb550d8845e4bba8a518417ccadd
msgid ""
"Lakeside has the same recorded clinical hours, bed-days, and completed "
"episodes under two pre-declared eligibility rules. A same service-contract "
"rule admits three hospitals and gives Lakeside a 6.25 percent common "
"proportional resource-saving opportunity, represented by a radial score of "
"0.9375, with North as its active peer. A shared district-mission rule also "
"admits West and gives Lakeside a 9.72 percent opportunity, represented by a "
"score of 0.9028, with North and West as active peers. Both opportunities "
"protect 100 completed episodes and precede slack completion. A final box "
"states that the difference is conditional and noncausal."
msgstr ""
"在两项预先声明的资格规则下，Lakeside 记录的临床工时、床日与既定病例保持相同。同服务合同规则纳入三家医院，给出 6.25% "
"的共同比例资源节约机会，对应径向得分 0.9375，North 是活跃参照单元。共同地区任务规则还纳入 West，给出 9.72% 的机会，对应得分 "
"0.9028，North 与 West 是活跃参照单元。两项机会均保护 100 个既定病例，且先于松弛调整。末框强调两者差异是条件性的，不具有因果含义。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:304
#: be98090750d54354af473785a67b233b
msgid ""
"Lakeside's observed operation does not change. The common proportional "
"resource-saving opportunity rises from 6.25 percent to 9.72 percent--a 3.47 "
"percentage-point sensitivity to the pre-declared eligible population. It "
"neither estimates a causal contract effect nor tests whether West's "
"practices will transfer or whether Lakeside's management is inferior."
msgstr ""
"Lakeside 的观测经营活动没有改变。共同比例资源节约机会从 6.25% 增至 9.72%，即对预先声明合格总体有 3.47 "
"个百分点的敏感性。它既不估计合同的因果效应，也不检验 West 的实践能否迁移，或 Lakeside 的管理是否更差。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:311
#: 6665fbc3f26b4a63b5c041cf900c15ef
msgid ""
"Neither rule is automatically correct. The narrow rule asks what Lakeside "
"can learn from hospitals under the same service contract. The broader rule "
"asks what it can learn across a shared district mission after the authority "
"has documented why West is institutionally comparable for this study. That "
"review must be completed before West's fitted intensity is known; excluding "
"West only after it becomes a demanding peer would be result-driven design. "
"Whether a practice will transfer in implementation remains a separate "
"question. The ordinary BCC account in the figure protects completed episodes"
" but does not include harm, so it cannot support a quality conclusion. "
"Because the fits request only the radial score, neither makes a Pareto--"
"Koopmans or slack-completed target claim."
msgstr ""
"两项规则都不会自动正确。窄规则询问 Lakeside 能从相同服务合同的医院学到什么；宽规则则在主管部门记录 West "
"对本研究为何具有制度可比性之后，询问它能从共同地区任务中学到什么。这项审查必须在知道 West 的拟合强度之前完成；只有在 West "
"成为严格比较对象之后才排除它，会使设计由结果驱动。实践能否真正迁移仍是另一个问题。图中的通常 BCC "
"核算保护既定病例，却没有纳入伤害，因此不能支持质量结论。由于拟合只要求径向得分，两者都没有作出 Pareto--"
"Koopmans 有效或松弛调整完成的目标主张。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:323
#: e3f8ae112df7434487e394d39cbf521c
msgid ""
"The difference therefore belongs in a sensitivity analysis, not a table of "
"causal effects. No contract was assigned to Lakeside and no hospital changed"
" its behaviour; only the body of evidence admitted to the comparison "
"changed."
msgstr "因此，这项差异应进入敏感性分析，而不是因果效应表。Lakeside 未被分配任何合同，医院也没有改变行为；变化的只有比较所允许的证据。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:327
#: 3b1f9b7c9bd14cb5a77880711d18c32a
msgid "Repeated peer selection is an audit lead, not a trophy"
msgstr "反复被选为活跃参照单元，是审计线索而不是奖杯"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:329
#: d12fc8ba8b5d4f589bc3257c9cec5ce5
msgid ""
"After the eligible population has been fixed, the authority may ask whether "
"the same organization keeps appearing in the comparator plans chosen for "
"different hospitals. A recurring peer has **comparative reach** in this "
"sample: its observed resource--service mix helps the model describe feasible"
" improvements for several organizations. That makes it a useful place to "
"begin an audit of data quality and operating practice. It does not make the "
"peer a winner."
msgstr "合格总体固定后，主管部门可以询问同一组织是否反复出现在不同医院的比较方案中。反复出现的活跃参照单元在本样本中具有**比较覆盖力**：其观测资源—服务组合帮助模型描述多个组织的可行改进。这使它成为核查数据质量与经营实践的合适起点，却不会使它自动成为赢家。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:337
#: 7a1d7dafcacc4eb6828da80842ad0a78
msgid ""
"Reference frequency simply counts appearances in the selected comparator "
"plans. Self-use is shown separately because an efficient organization will "
"often select itself in ordinary self-inclusive DEA. The more informative "
"question is how often an organization contributes to plans for *other* "
"organizations. Adding the fitted intensity values across different plans "
"would not improve this diagnostic; each intensity belongs to a different "
"comparison and has no common unit across hospitals."
msgstr ""
"参照频数只统计在所选比较方案中出现的次数。单独显示自我参照，是因为在通常包含自身的 DEA "
"中，有效率的组织往往选择自身。更有信息的问题，是一个组织对*其他*组织的方案贡献了多少次。把不同方案中的拟合强度相加不会改善诊断；每个强度属于不同的比较，在医院之间没有共同单位。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:345
#: 4ff5b8805b734bde851979e76d78cac0
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The eight-organization service case in {numref}`fig-reference-frequency-"
"reader` uses the book's `slacks_2x2` teaching data and an input-oriented BCC"
" fit. Organizations A--D lie on the fitted boundary. C appears in its own "
"plan and in four plans for other organizations; B appears in its own and "
"three others. D appears once for another organization, while A appears only "
"for itself. B and C therefore have wider comparative reach in this "
"particular fit. The count tells the authority where to investigate, not what"
" it will find there."
msgstr ""
"{numref}`fig-reference-frequency-reader` 中的八组织服务案例采用本书 `slacks_2x2` "
"教学数据和投入导向 BCC 拟合。A--D 位于拟合边界。C 出现在自身方案以及四个其他组织的方案中；B 出现在自身和三个其他组织中；D "
"被一个其他组织选中，A 只出现在自身方案。因此，B 与 C "
"在这一特定拟合中具有更广的比较覆盖力。频数告诉主管部门从哪里开始调查，并不预先决定会发现什么。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:353
#: 0373b3692fa14eaca6c3aa971ebe9261
msgid ""
"Horizontal stacked bars separate self-reference from selection by other "
"organizations for eight service organizations. A appears only in its own "
"plan, B is selected by three others, C by four others, D by one other, and E"
" through H do not appear in the selected plans."
msgstr ""
"水平堆叠条形图区分八个服务组织的自我参照与被其他组织选中。A 只出现在自身方案中，B 被三个其他组织选中，C 被四个其他组织选中，D "
"被一个其他组织选中，E 至 H 未出现在所选方案中。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:358
#: f5d584f6e6ab4df4b9e8ea5a798c27f5
msgid ""
"Repeated selection identifies comparative reach in one fitted sample. It is "
"a prompt to investigate measurement quality and possible practice "
"transferability, not a ranking of management quality."
msgstr "反复入选只说明一个拟合样本中的比较覆盖力；它提示调查测量质量与实践迁移可能性，不是管理质量排名。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:363
#: 40c5a2f75f53434f85f071d2b76f1ad4
msgid "The same audit can be reproduced directly from the fitted result:"
msgstr "同一项审计可以直接由拟合结果重现："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:391
#: 12d6f8966bdd4f029378d7ffb3e06df5
msgid ""
"The four boundary organizations all have a radial score of one, yet their "
"frequencies differ. Frequency is therefore neither another efficiency score "
"nor a quality-adjusted league table. E--H do not appear in the plans shown, "
"but they remain eligible evidence and could matter under another defensible "
"model or another equally good comparator plan. A high count likewise says "
"nothing by itself about superiority, causation, or whether a practice can be"
" transferred to a hospital with a different workforce, mission, regulation, "
"or service obligation."
msgstr ""
"四个边界组织的径向得分都等于 1，频数却不同。因此，频数既不是另一种效率得分，也不是质量调整排行榜。E--H "
"没有出现在图示方案中，但仍是合格证据，在另一项可辩护模型或另一个同样优的比较方案中可能发挥作用。高频数本身也不表示优越性、因果关系，或实践能够迁移到具有不同人员、任务、监管或服务责任的医院。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:400
#: e9ef2396f9544b819ad2607a7334df30
msgid ""
"The sensible next step is investigation rather than an award. Verify the "
"recurrent organization's data and variable roles, study the practices behind"
" its resource--service mix, and ask whether they are institutionally "
"comparable and transferable. Then test whether the substantive finding "
"survives peer and model sensitivities chosen in advance. Deleting a hospital"
" merely because it is a demanding recurrent peer would redefine the study "
"after seeing the answer."
msgstr "合理的下一步是调查，而不是颁奖：核实反复出现组织的数据和变量角色，研究其资源—服务组合背后的实践，询问其制度可比性与可迁移性，再检验实质结论能否经受预先选定的比较对象与模型敏感性。仅因某家医院是严格且反复出现的比较对象就删除它，会在看到答案后重新定义研究。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:408
#: 5d02db25c5674c2db96ed0fbd19f3f54
msgid ""
"Eligibility also has a dimensional consequence. The full data-role "
"declaration below contains two inputs, one desirable output, one undesirable"
" output, and only three same-contract hospitals. The two score comparisons "
"deliberately leave harm outside the radial account and contain only three or"
" four eligible hospitals. Neither setup is large enough for a persuasive "
"empirical frontier. Additional variables often make more observations appear"
" efficient because each organization gains another dimension in which to "
"distinguish itself. A larger model is not automatically a richer "
"explanation. Theory, measurement quality, sample support, and stability "
"should determine whether a variable remains."
msgstr "资格还有维度后果。下面完整的数据角色声明包含两项投入、一项合意产出、一项非合意产出，以及仅三家同合同医院。两项得分比较有意把伤害留在径向核算之外，且分别只有三家或四家合格医院。两种设定都不足以形成有说服力的经验前沿。增加变量常会让更多观测显得有效率，因为每个组织多了一个展示差异的维度。更大的模型不会自动带来更丰富的解释；应由理论、测量质量、样本支持与稳定性决定是否保留变量。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:419
#: d27015648f514107bc6d59bcb0985a97
msgid ""
"Sample size is therefore not a purely numerical hurdle. The relevant support"
" comes from comparable observations that occupy informative parts of the "
"resource--service space. Hundreds of hospital-years do not provide hundreds "
"of independent organizational comparisons if they repeat a small number of "
"sites under nearly unchanged conditions. Conversely, a large administrative "
"database does not repair a thin eligible comparison population for a "
"specialized hospital. The empirical question is whether the eligible "
"evidence can support the frontier and the distinctions the study asks it to "
"make."
msgstr "因此，样本规模不只是数值门槛。真正的支持来自在资源—服务空间中占据有信息位置的可比观测。如果数百个医院—年度只是在几乎不变的条件下重复少数院区，就不能提供数百项独立组织比较。反过来，大型行政数据库也不能修补专科医院稀薄的合格比较总体。经验问题在于，合格证据能否支持研究要求的前沿和区分。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:429
#: 626e53f7c45e4b2c8eaaada0f26e7e61
msgid ""
"At this point the authority should be able to tell one coherent story "
"without referring to a score: who is accountable, over what period, for "
"which resources and services; which burdens are jointly produced; which "
"conditions lie beyond managerial control; how every quantity is measured; "
"and why each eligible hospital supplies relevant evidence. It should also be"
" able to say what kind of conclusion the evidence could support. If any "
"answer depends on seeing which specification produces the most convenient "
"result, the study is not yet ready to be fitted."
msgstr "此时，主管部门应能在不提得分的情况下讲出一条连贯故事：谁在什么时期对哪些资源与服务负责；哪些负担被联合生产；哪些条件超出管理控制；每个数量如何测量；每家合格医院为何提供相关证据；以及证据能够支持哪类结论。如果任何答案取决于哪个设定给出最方便的结果，研究还没有准备好拟合。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:438
#: 26822e7def3d449b8dd7c7328c19812f
msgid "Make the economic account visible in the data"
msgstr "让经济核算在数据中清楚可见"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:440
#: a47b716b0b1545a4ba8ddaedcba21534
msgid ""
"The following teaching data are deliberately small. They show how the "
"authority's economic account and eligibility rule become visible in code; "
"they are not offered as an adequate hospital study. Notice that the complete"
" candidate roster is retained even though only eligible rows enter the DEA "
"comparison."
msgstr ""
"下面的教学数据有意保持很小，用于展示主管部门的经济核算和资格规则如何呈现在代码中，并不构成充分的医院研究。请注意，完整候选名单会一直保留，即使只有合格行进入"
" DEA 比较。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:531
#: 8b9f058f53a54311b7708dab6e6bc3ec
msgid ""
"The declaration makes several conceptual mistakes harder to hide. Each "
"organization must have a unique identity, its production quantities must be "
"measured consistently, and one quantity cannot simultaneously play "
"conflicting economic roles. Keeping the role names visible also helps "
"managers connect later results to the original resource, service, and harm "
"account."
msgstr "这项声明使若干概念错误更难隐藏。每个组织必须有唯一身份，生产数量必须按一致口径测量，同一数量不能同时承担相互冲突的经济角色。保留可见的角色名称，也有助于管理者把后续结果与最初的资源、服务和伤害核算联系起来。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:537
#: 49369583287b43f5baa53c144c372c3b
msgid ""
"It does not complete the study. The data declaration cannot decide whether "
"harm is strongly or weakly disposable, whether inputs should contract, "
"whether VRS or CRS is credible, or why the retained hospitals may be "
"compared. `same_contract_eligible` records an explicit research decision "
"made before performance is calculated; it is not an active-peer result "
"learned from favourable scores. The context columns remain in "
"`hospital_frame` so that the institutional explanation for inclusion and "
"exclusion stays visible, rather than being silently converted into "
"production inputs."
msgstr ""
"但声明并未完成研究。数据声明不能决定伤害采用强处置还是弱处置、投入是否应收缩、VRS 还是 CRS "
"可信，也不能解释保留的医院为何可以比较。`same_contract_eligible` "
"记录的是绩效计算前作出的明确研究决定，不是从有利得分中学习到的活跃参照结果。情境列仍保留在 `hospital_frame` "
"中，使纳入与排除的制度解释保持可见，而不是被悄悄转成生产投入。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:546
#: 45c1ccd12d9c49a39c278b0a24c9cbb7
msgid ""
"`role_declared_data` contains avoidable harm by design. An ordinary `BCC` "
"fit will stop with a specification error rather than silently decide how "
"that harm can be disposed. The next block deliberately constructs a narrower"
" resource--service account for the ordinary BCC comparison. It leaves harm "
"outside that score; it does not turn harm into an input or authorize a "
"quality conclusion."
msgstr ""
"`role_declared_data` 有意包含可避免伤害。通常的 `BCC` 拟合会以设定错误停止，而不会默默决定伤害如何处置。下一代码块有意为通常"
" BCC 比较构造较窄的资源—服务核算。它把伤害留在该得分之外；既没有把伤害变成投入，也没有授权得出质量结论。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:553
#: 74e279a6a73a4968b772a18f8b58689f
msgid ""
"The figure's two narrow resource accounts can be reproduced without turning "
"mission or environment into inputs. Each declared population gets its own "
"`DEAData` object, while the complete candidate roster remains available for "
"substantive review:"
msgstr "图中的两项窄资源核算可以重现，而不把任务或环境转成投入。每个已声明总体都有自己的 `DEAData` 对象，完整候选名单仍可用于实质审查："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:591
#: 81477538f3834c00ba5cd63d41d12740
msgid ""
"The two fitted comparisons return 0.9375 for Lakeside under the same-"
"contract population and 0.902778 under the district-mission population. For "
"this input-oriented radial account, the score is the common resource-"
"retention factor. Its complement therefore translates the first result into "
"a 6.25 percent common proportional resource-saving opportunity and the "
"second into a 9.72 percent opportunity, in both cases while protecting "
"completed episodes. These are phase-one opportunities before slack "
"completion, not instructions to cut either resource by that amount."
msgstr ""
"两项拟合对 Lakeside 的返回值分别为：同合同总体下 0.9375，地区任务总体下 "
"0.902778。对于投入导向径向核算，得分是共同资源保留因子，因此其补数把第一个结果转为 6.25% 的共同比例资源节约机会，把第二个转为 "
"9.72%，两者都保护既定病例。这些是完成松弛调整之前的第一阶段机会，不是要求任何资源按该比例削减的指令。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:600
#: 02f8072d636541afabea52e50db29b6d
msgid ""
"In the latter fit, the positive intensities are $4/9$ for North and $5/9$ "
"for West. Those intensities identify the selected phase-one comparator; they"
" do not establish a completed target, prove that West's contract has no "
"operational consequence, or prescribe copying either hospital. Scores from "
"the two eligibility rules should be reported side by side, not averaged into"
" a supposedly more robust number. The side-by-side account preserves the "
"substantive reason the estimates differ."
msgstr ""
"在后一拟合中，North 的正强度为 $4/9$，West 为 $5/9$。这些强度识别所选第一阶段比较方案，不能确立完整目标，也不能证明 West "
"的合同没有经营后果，或规定照搬任何一家医院。两项资格规则的得分应并列报告，而不能平均成一个所谓更稳健的数值；并列核算保留了估计差异的实质原因。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:608
#: 064faf3c0a51409595bcd77cab291b4e
msgid ""
"In a real project, the variable record should also retain units, time basis,"
" source system, transformations, missing-data policy, quality checks, and "
"the managerial owner of each quantity. “Staff” is not a sufficient "
"definition if one hospital reports paid full-time equivalents and another "
"reports worked hours including agency staff. Nor is “annual” sufficient if "
"financial years, calendar years, and rolling twelve-month windows are mixed."
msgstr "在真实项目中，变量记录还应保留单位、时间口径、源系统、转换、缺失数据政策、质量检查和每个数量的管理责任人。如果一家医院报告付薪全职当量，另一家报告包含派遣人员的实际工时，“人员”就不是充分定义；如果财年、日历年和滚动十二个月窗口混在一起，“年度”也不是充分定义。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:615
#: 7ff3f3cd74e3453183780979166f85bf
msgid "Only then choose the method family"
msgstr "只有到这一步，才选择方法族"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:617
#: b5120a9617c243ccb63c20b52594ec50
msgid ""
"Once the boundary, roles, horizon, and eligible population are credible, the"
" board's question can be matched to a model. Orientation should protect the "
"declared commitment and place adjustment on quantities the responsible "
"manager can change. Returns to scale state whether proportional replication "
"is treated as attainable and whether managers are being held responsible for"
" operating scale. Neither choice should be made because it produces a more "
"appealing league table."
msgstr "当边界、角色、期限和合格总体都可信时，董事会的问题才能与模型匹配。导向应保护已声明承诺，并把调整放在责任管理者可以改变的数量上。规模报酬说明按比例复制是否视为可实现，以及管理者是否对经营规模负责。两项选择都不能只因某个选项给出更好看的排行榜而作出。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:625
#: fbf242aa9f444e368ab99598182f8aac
msgid ""
"If the study excludes harm and asks how much controllable resource could be "
"saved while preserving completed care, an input-oriented radial or nonradial"
" model may be a natural starting point. The next chapter shows how eligible "
"observations become an empirical production technology under assumptions "
"about mixing, disposal, and scale."
msgstr "如果研究排除伤害，并询问在保留既定诊疗的同时可以节约多少可控资源，投入导向径向或非径向模型可以作为自然起点。下一章说明合格观测如何在混合、处置与规模假设下形成经验生产技术。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:631
#: 303808368b4b4304af0a18cf9aa44261
msgid ""
"Keep the strict same-contract rule fixed and the board can ask several "
"useful questions without changing who is allowed to supply evidence. A "
"radial account asks whether Lakeside could reduce both controllable "
"resources at one common rate while protecting completed care. A slacks-based"
" account asks whether the shortfall is uneven--perhaps bed-days can be "
"reduced more than clinical hours, or an additional service gain remains "
"after one resource has stopped improving. A directional account asks whether"
" a programme agreed in advance, such as saving a stated number of clinical "
"hours and bed-days while adding a stated number of completed episodes, is "
"attainable as a package. Lakeside, North, and East remain the admitted "
"evidence in all three accounts; the model may select different active "
"comparator plans because the operating commitments differ."
msgstr ""
"保持严格的同合同规则不变，董事会无需改变谁能提供证据，就能提出多个有用问题。径向核算询问 Lakeside "
"能否在保护既定诊疗时按同一比率减少两项可控资源；基于松弛变量的核算询问不足是否不均匀，例如床日能否比临床工时减少更多，或某项资源停止改善后服务仍有增加空间；方向性核算则询问一项事先商定的方案——例如节约给定数量的临床工时与床日，同时增加给定数量的既定病例——能否整体实现。三种核算都只允许"
" Lakeside、North 与 East 提供证据；由于经营承诺不同，模型可能选择不同活跃比较方案。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:644
#: 0b6f51a3136045be889c1131ca5a89db
msgid ""
"These are not three votes on one hidden notion of performance. The radial "
"finding concerns a common percentage, the slacks-based finding concerns "
"resource- and service-specific gaps, and the directional finding concerns "
"the declared programme. Holding the comparison-right rule constant helps the"
" board see that differences come from the management question rather than an"
" unannounced change of comparison population. None of the three findings "
"proves that an admitted hospital is superior, that its practices caused the "
"gap, or that its operating arrangements can be transferred to Lakeside."
msgstr ""
"这不是对某个隐藏绩效概念的三次投票。径向结论涉及共同百分比；基于松弛变量的结论涉及各资源与服务特定的差距；方向性结论涉及已声明方案。固定比较资格规则，使董事会清楚看到差异来自管理问题，而非未说明的比较总体变化。三种结论都不能证明纳入的医院更优、其实践造成差距，或其经营安排能够迁移到"
" Lakeside。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:653
#: 77576046d13a4c908bcd8cc53d12203a
msgid ""
"If harm remains part of the conclusion, an ordinary BCC technology is not "
"the same study with one extra column. The analysis must move to Part III and"
" declare how desirable care and harm are jointly attainable and reducible. "
"If diagnosis, treatment, and discharge must agree on internal patient flows,"
" a network model in Part V represents that organizational structure. If "
"waiting lists, capacity, or obligations connect years, Part VI treats the "
"hospital as an operating history. If rural and urban hospitals face distinct"
" opportunity sets, Part VII separates within-group performance from the gap "
"between represented group opportunities."
msgstr ""
"如果伤害仍属于结论的一部分，通常 BCC "
"技术并不是简单多加一列的同一研究。分析必须进入第三篇，声明合意医疗与伤害如何联合实现和减少。如果诊断、治疗和出院必须保持内部患者流一致，第五篇的网络模型表示这一组织结构；如果候诊名单、产能或义务连接不同年份，第六篇把医院视为一条经营历程；如果乡村与城市医院面对不同的生产机会集合，第七篇则分开群组内部表现与被代表群组机会之间的差距。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:663
#: b709cdaa26304016817f6ae35dd6c57c
msgid ""
"This is not an automatic model selector. The production story still has to "
"justify the maintained assumptions. The map simply helps prevent a technical"
" setting from silently changing the management question."
msgstr "这不是自动模型选择器。生产故事仍须为既定假设辩护；这张地图只是防止技术设置悄悄改变管理问题。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:667
#: 1fc62c5e189341a89d8afe1c29f428aa
msgid "Read the eventual score inside its comparison contract"
msgstr "把最终得分放回比较契约中阅读"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:669
#: 7f775258a2c0415290edcead1a8b09f3
msgid ""
"Suppose a later model reports that Lakeside could retain only 90 percent of "
"its controllable resources while preserving completed care. A responsible "
"statement would identify the conditions:"
msgstr "假设后续模型报告 Lakeside 在保留既定诊疗时只需保留 90% 的可控资源。一项负责任的陈述应明确条件："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:673
#: c8e610fbb816432087be138abdd6b74e
msgid ""
"Relative to the eligible district hospitals measured under the common "
"episode definition, and under an input-oriented VRS production technology, "
"Lakeside's benchmark supports a ten-percent common reduction in controllable"
" resources while preserving its recorded risk-adjusted completed-care "
"commitment."
msgstr ""
"相对于采用共同病例定义计量的合格地区医院，并在投入导向 VRS 生产技术下，Lakeside 的标杆支持在保留其记录的风险调整后既定诊疗承诺时，共同减少"
" 10% 的可控资源。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:679
#: eb42d1d629784050b0947fcd7cf0c10b
msgid ""
"The sentence is intentionally narrower than “Lakeside should cut its budget "
"by ten percent.” DEA has not priced the transition, established a causal "
"management failure, measured unrecorded aspects of care quality, or shown "
"that the comparator plan can be implemented locally. Peers explain why the "
"model treats a plan as attainable and may point toward organizational "
"learning; they are not instructions to imitate every practice."
msgstr ""
"这句话有意比“Lakeside 应削减 10% 预算”更窄。DEA "
"没有为转型定价，没有确立管理失败的因果关系，没有测量未记录的医疗质量，也没有证明比较方案可以在当地实施。活跃参照单元解释模型为何把方案视为可实现，并可能指向组织学习方向，却不是照搬全部实践的指令。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:686
#: 00931f3194704022817201b1dabde85d
msgid ""
"Targets require the same caution. A target may combine several hospitals' "
"activities under convexity. That combination is evidence about attainable "
"resource--service quantities only when divisibility or portfolio mixing is "
"credible. It is not a literal proposal to merge hospitals. Several optimal "
"targets may support the same score, and engineering, workforce, legal, and "
"political constraints can distinguish an implementable plan from a model-"
"supported benchmark. DEA can identify the size and composition of a "
"benchmark opportunity; implementation analysis asks how, at what cost, and "
"under whose authority it could be pursued."
msgstr ""
"目标方案同样需要谨慎。凸性下的目标可以组合多家医院的活动；只有当活动可分或组合经营可信时，这种组合才是可实现资源—服务数量的证据，而不是合并医院的字面建议。多个最优目标可以支持相同得分，工程、人员、法律和政治约束也会使可实施方案区别于模型支持的标杆。DEA"
" 能识别标杆机会的规模和构成；实施分析则询问如何、以何种成本、在谁的权限下推进。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:696
#: bd68cfa92bc34c759d0029bc573d17dc
msgid ""
"The most useful management interpretation therefore keeps four layers "
"visible:"
msgstr "因此，最有用的管理解释会同时保留四层内容："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:699
#: 95b180603bef42d79e23b86e6d8d2350
msgid ""
"the study design--unit boundary, horizon, eligible comparison population, "
"variable roles, and production assumptions;"
msgstr "研究设计——分析单元边界、期限、合格比较总体、变量角色与生产假设；"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:701
#: 110741f3d10646ea96ae55fb5aaa328d
msgid ""
"the performance finding--the defined measure, its direction, and the "
"comparison it supports;"
msgstr "绩效结论——定义明确的测度、数值方向及其支持的比较；"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:703
#: 8e0aeaa2b6444ddc83f29e1f033a6829
msgid ""
"the operating evidence--targets, shortfalls, peers, and any alternative "
"optima; and"
msgstr "经营证据——目标方案、不足、活跃参照单元和任何替代最优解；以及"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:705
#: de59de926dc847e3b19b62c1463157bc
msgid ""
"the conclusion boundary--what remains unmeasured, uncertain, or outside "
"managerial control."
msgstr "结论边界——仍未测量、具有不确定性或超出管理控制的内容。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:708
#: 6853b432f13346fcb987fd94b64f8267
msgid "From a sample benchmark to a research conclusion"
msgstr "从样本标杆走向研究结论"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:710
#: 93f8670301874f7b8e348c3feaba19bf
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Suppose Lakeside's score is available to ten decimal places. Those decimals "
"describe the comparison defined by these hospitals, variables, and "
"production assumptions. They do not establish that the same frontier would "
"appear in another credible sample, after a measurement revision, or in the "
"wider population of hospitals. DEA constructs its frontier from a finite set"
" of observed practices, so sampling variation and the identity of the "
"eligible reference population remain part of the evidence "
"{cite:p}`simar1998,simar2000,kneip2008`."
msgstr ""
"假设 Lakeside "
"的得分精确到小数点后十位。这些小数只描述由这些医院、变量和生产假设界定的比较，并不能证明在另一个可信样本、测量修订后或更广泛医院总体中会出现同一前沿。DEA"
" 由有限观测实践构造前沿，因此抽样变动与合格参照总体的具体构成仍是证据的一部分 "
"{cite:p}`simar1998,simar2000,kneip2008`。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:719
#: fa8d6b9c941745aab4d53e89bb582eb7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"An unusually strong hospital may therefore have considerable influence on "
"many results. Influence is not proof of error: the hospital may demonstrate "
"a genuinely transferable practice. Nor should an inconvenient observation be"
" removed merely because it creates demanding targets. The sensible response "
"is to check its source data and units, reconsider its eligibility against "
"the study design chosen in advance, and then show how important conclusions "
"change under defensible alternative eligible populations. If one valid "
"hospital determines much of the frontier, the study should describe that "
"sparse support rather than conceal it behind extra decimal places. If the "
"record is erroneous or institutionally incomparable, its correction or "
"exclusion is a data or design decision and should be explained as such "
"{cite:p}`dyson2001`."
msgstr ""
"一所异常优秀的医院可能对许多结果有很大影响。影响力不证明错误：它可能展示真正可迁移的实践；也不能仅因某项观测形成严格目标就将其删除。合理做法是核查源数据与单位，按事先确定的研究设计重新审视其资格，再展示重要结论在可辩护的替代合格总体下如何变化。如果一家有效医院决定大部分前沿，研究应说明支持稀疏，而不是用更多小数位掩盖。如果记录有误或制度上不可比，修正或排除就是数据或设计决定，应据实说明"
" {cite:p}`dyson2001`。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:731
#: 3a74ef9fe66f46fb995dc2c6149a6296
msgid "It helps to distinguish four levels of claim:"
msgstr "可以把主张区分为四个层次："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:353
#: 37da269e416741b9b520df29433dfaf4
msgid "Claim"
msgstr "主张"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:353
#: a859595d963941689b7d524814f460eb
msgid "What the study needs"
msgstr "研究需要什么"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:353
#: a4f5e186f953475b8b842857f786b260
msgid "**Conditional sample benchmark**"
msgstr "**条件性样本标杆**"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:353
#: c61502823ce140ca8532965082486ca4
msgid "a correctly specified DEA comparison and a fully stated study design"
msgstr "设定正确的 DEA 比较和完整陈述的研究设计"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:353
#: 00cfccdace2d4871bdc323228f3da48f
msgid "**Stable empirical finding**"
msgstr "**稳定的经验结论**"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:353
#: a950206332d6462489480312d6074b66
msgid ""
"data-quality checks and pre-specified sensitivity to influential "
"observations, variables, and the eligible comparison population"
msgstr "数据质量检查，以及对有影响力观测、变量和合格比较总体的预先设定敏感性分析"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:353
#: ea92f9b922ed4f20b5088674eed3f26f
msgid "**Population statement**"
msgstr "**总体陈述**"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:353
#: cb646657b3f5496f883be4e522616cf8
msgid ""
"an explicit sampling model and an inferential procedure valid for the chosen"
" frontier estimator"
msgstr "明确的抽样模型，以及对所选前沿估计量有效的推断程序"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:353
#: dd7c06ba500b475fbe5ab45017ebef54
msgid "**Causal management statement**"
msgstr "**因果管理陈述**"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:353
#: 4ccfa91d08504806a6ada4ee478d7513
msgid ""
"a separate identification design showing what would happen under an "
"intervention"
msgstr "单独的识别设计，用于说明实施干预后会发生什么"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:740
#: 5b4b2207207c41d68c77af39e1291f95
msgid ""
"The last two levels do not follow automatically from the first. Bootstrap "
"methods can quantify particular forms of sampling uncertainty and finite-"
"sample bias, but only under a stated data-generating process and conditions "
"appropriate to the estimator. They are not a universal resampling switch, "
"and their confidence intervals do not absorb coding errors, omitted "
"outcomes, or an indefensible peer definition."
msgstr ""
"后两个层次不会由第一个自动推出。Bootstrap "
"方法可以量化特定形式的抽样不确定性和有限样本偏差，但必须有已声明的数据生成过程和适合该估计量的条件。它不是通用的重抽样开关，其置信区间也不会吸收编码错误、遗漏结果或无法辩护的比较对象定义。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:747
#: 685f4554503b4116bf106464881d8dbb
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Contextual conditions require one further distinction. Deprivation or rural "
"remoteness may change the production opportunities available to a hospital; "
"alternatively, hospitals may share one opportunity set while such conditions"
" are associated with how close they operate to it. The first account calls "
"for a design that changes or conditions the frontier--for example, justified"
" peer groups, a metafrontier, or a conditional frontier. A second-stage "
"analysis addresses a different question and relies on a separability "
"assumption that the contextual variables do not themselves alter the "
"attainable boundary {cite:p}`daraio2005,simar2007`."
msgstr ""
"情境条件还需要进一步区分。贫困或乡村偏远可能改变医院可获得的生产机会；另一种可能是医院共享同一机会集合，而这些条件只与其接近该集合的程度相关。前一种核算要求改变或条件化前沿的设计，例如有依据的比较群组、共同前沿或条件前沿；第二阶段分析回答另一问题，并依赖情境变量本身不改变可实现边界的可分性假设"
" {cite:p}`daraio2005,simar2007`。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:757
#: 457eb44e88934422a29000b14bb85107
msgid ""
"For this reason, regressing estimated DEA scores mechanically on contextual "
"variables with ordinary least squares or Tobit is unsafe. The scores are "
"jointly generated by the same estimated frontier, have finite-sample bias, "
"and are not made into independent observations merely because they lie in a "
"bounded interval. A statistically coherent second stage must state its data-"
" generating process and justify its inferential procedure. Even then, an "
"association between remoteness and efficiency is not the causal effect of "
"remoteness, funding, or management. Causal language requires assumptions and"
" evidence beyond the DEA comparison."
msgstr ""
"因此，用普通最小二乘或 Tobit 机械回归估计的 DEA "
"得分并不安全。得分由同一估计前沿共同产生，存在有限样本偏差，也不会仅因落在有界区间就成为相互独立的观测。统计上连贯的第二阶段必须声明数据生成过程，并为推断程序辩护。即便如此，偏远与效率之间的关联也不是偏远、资金或管理的因果效应；因果语言需要"
" DEA 比较之外的假设和证据。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:767
#: d073f2cf9bbd40c8a770f3bcc53993c6
msgid ""
"Sensitivity analysis should vary defensible assumptions, not search for a "
"preferred conclusion. For the hospital study, the authority might compare a "
"core urban cohort with a pre-specified environment-sensitive design, examine"
" whether bed-days are adjustable over alternative horizons, and test whether"
" the result survives justified case-mix and quality definitions. Each "
"version should retain its own interpretation; averaging their scores would "
"not remove the underlying disagreement."
msgstr "敏感性分析应改变可辩护的假设，而不是搜索偏好的结论。对于医院研究，主管部门可以比较核心城市群体与预先设定的环境敏感设计，审查床日在不同期限内是否可调整，并检验结果能否经受有依据的病例组合与质量定义。每个版本都应保留自己的解释；平均其得分不会消除背后的分歧。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/02-study-design.md:775
#: 40b6fa31ed374ecfa74fb38273f878d1
msgid ""
"The next chapter begins where this design work ends. Given a set of eligible"
" organizations and production quantities, it asks which additional operating"
" plans the observed evidence should make attainable. Convexity, "
"disposability, and returns to scale will turn the eligibility ledger into an"
" empirical production technology--and will make clear why choosing the "
"comparison population was already part of the economic model."
msgstr "下一章从这些设计工作结束的地方开始。在给定一组合格组织与生产数量后，它询问观测证据还应使哪些经营方案可实现。凸性、可处置性和规模报酬会把资格台账转化为经验生产技术，也会清楚表明：选择比较总体本来就是经济模型的一部分。"
